{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 proof of the main results of A. Languasco, J. Pintz and A. Zaccagnini, On the sum of two primes and k powers of two, Bull. London Math. Soc. 39, 2007, pages 771 to 780, conditional on three results of the literature that the paper cites. For k >= 1 the entry proves that all but O of X^{3/5} times log X to the power 10 even N <= X are sums of two primes and k powers of two; the paper's main theorem, the asymptotic formula for the weighted number of such representations outside an exceptional set of the same size, on the even N in J of X = [2X/3, X], with the main term coefficient 2 c0 C of k and N, where c0 is the twin prime constant; and Corollary 4.2 of the paper on the major arcs. The three cited inputs are explicit hypotheses, never axioms: the explicit formula of Lemma 4.1 of the paper, which it quotes from J. Pintz, ELAZ 2004, Theorem 10; the zero density theorem of M. Jutila 1977, Theorem 1, display 1.8, as printed; and the zero free region of H. Iwaniec 1974, Theorem 2, page 97, as printed, read for nonreal characters. The real zero bound for real characters, which the paper cites from Pintz 1976 and Goldfeld and Schinzel 1975, is proved here from Siegel's theorem. The coefficient 2 c0 C of k and N is the one that the paper's own display 2 gives; the printed theorem states C of k and N in [1, 2] and omits the factor 2 c0, and the entry does not claim the range [1, 2]. Binary Goldbach, the case k = 0, is open and is not claimed. AI agents wrote the Lean code, Claude by Anthropic with a few leaves from other lab provers listed in PORTING.md, and it is offered for human audit.",
